==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|wurgen}}, {{m|gmh|worgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|wurgan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*wurgijaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*werǵʰ-|t=bind, squeeze}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|wurgen}}, {{m|nl|worgen}}, {{cog|en|worry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvʏʁɡən/|[ˈvʏɐ̯ɡŋ̍]}}
* {{audio|de|De-würgen.ogg|Audio}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[strangle]], to [[choke]]
#: {{ux|de|Die Krawatte ist so eng, dass sie mich '''würgt'''.|The tie is so tight that it's '''choking''' me.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|''[''{{m|de|an|t=on}} + dative'']''}} to [[gag]], to [[choke]], to [[retch]]
#: {{ux|de|Ich habe an einem Samen '''gewürgt'''.|I was '''choking''' on a seed.}}

